# Dataset: Pima Indians Diabetes

This dataset contains diagnostic information for female patients of Pima Indian heritage aged 21 and older. It is commonly used for binary classification tasks to predict whether a patient shows signs of diabetes based on features such as:

- Number of pregnancies
- Glucose level
- Blood pressure
- Skin thickness
- Insulin level
- Body mass index (BMI)
- Diabetes pedigree function
- Age

# Source
Originally sourced from the National Institute of Diabetes and Digestive and Kidney Diseases (NIDDK).  
Available on: [Kaggle - Pima Indians Diabetes Database](https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/uciml/pima-indians-diabetes-database)

# Format
- CSV file with 768 rows and 9 columns
- Target column: `Outcome` (1 = diabetes, 0 = no diabetes)
